  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The gust lines, the cone's ripple, where the dust and leaves fly and the swept mark's streaks vary per cast. The 0.32 s draw-in and the arrival at about 0.47 s stay fixed so the push lands on the same frame."
  },
  "director_notes": "A basic wind gust that pushes, a staple of air magic; the look is original. Choices: (1) a short 0.32 s draw-in (closing ring, wisps into the palm) so even a quick spell telegraphs; (2) the gust is a beam with style wind: a widening, mostly see-through cone of streaky air with pale gust lines rushing through it, because air is only visible through motion lines and what it carries; (3) the push is sold at the target by a rolling dust wave, leaves blown up and away and grit skittering, plus a light shake; (4) a swept decal fans along the cast direction (rotation 0) so the top view shows which way the wind went; (5) sound: a high quick wind for the draw-in, a whoosh, a bright wind for the gust, a soft wind as it settles. Nothing is additive: wind doesn't glow."
}
